.TH TOGGLY-MIGRATE 1 "2026-10-03" "Toggly CLI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
toggly-migrate \- Import feature flags from other platforms into Toggly
.SH SYNOPSIS
toggly\-cli migrate <command>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Import feature flags from other platforms into Toggly
.SS unleash
Import an Unleash export or Admin API feature list into a Toggly app and
environment\&. Default is dry\-run (compatibility report only); pass \-\-apply
to create missing features and set environment filters\&.
.PP
.B toggly\-cli migrate unleash \-\-file <path> \-\-app <appId> \-\-environment <env> [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-apply]
.SH OPTIONS
Options for migrate unleash:
.TP
.B \-\-file
Path to Unleash export JSON (or Admin API features payload)
.TP
.B \-\-app, \-\-application\-id
Application id (or set via 'toggly context set \-\-app')
.TP
.B \-\-environment, \-\-env
Toggly environment to import into (also selects Unleash environment slices
when present)
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Parse and print a compatibility report without API mutations (default when
\-\-apply is omitted)
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Create missing features and set environment filters via the Toggly API (does
not require a prior dry\-run)
.PP
Global options (all commands):
.TP
.B \-\-client\-id
OAuth2 client ID (or set TOGGLY_CLIENT_ID)
.TP
.B \-\-client\-secret
OAuth2 client secret (or set TOGGLY_CLIENT_SECRET)
.TP
.B \-\-authority
OAuth2 authority URL (defaults to https://auth\&.toggly\&.io)
.TP
.B \-\-base\-url
Base URL for Toggly API (defaults to https://app\&.toggly\&.io/api)
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine\-readable camelCase JSON instead of human text
.SH EXAMPLES
.B toggly\-cli migrate unleash \-\-file export\&.json \-\-app <app\-id>
.B \-\-env Production
.PP
